{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block body %}
{% include '_processing_banner.html.twig' %}
<section class="hero">
    <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">MemorialAtlas</span>
        <h1>Lives remembered.<br>Stories connected.</h1>
        <p>From gravestone photographs to a searchable record of remembrance.</p>
        <p>A name, a date, “beloved father,” a shared life. Cemetery inscriptions preserve connections between people and the places they called home. MemorialAtlas helps families, researchers and communities find those details and return to the photographs behind them.</p>
        <a class="button" href="{{ path('item_search') }}">Search the collection</a>
    </div>
    {% if heroImage %}<figure><twig:ux:image :src="heroImage.thumbnailSource" width="600" alt="A gravestone from the MemorialAtlas collection" /><figcaption>Every record begins with a photograph. Every reading remains open to review.</figcaption></figure>{% endif %}
</section>
<section style="max-width:800px">
<h2>A camera roll is only the beginning.</h2>
<p>A walk through a cemetery might produce hundreds of photographs: a whole headstone, a close-up of a faded date, another face of the same monument. It can be hard to tell where one memorial ends and the next begins, let alone find a particular person later.</p>
<p>MemorialAtlas brings those pieces together. It reads inscriptions, helps identify photographs of the same marker, and organizes the text into names, dates and relationship clues that you can search.</p>
<h2>Keep the evidence in view.</h2>
<p>A shared surname is a clue, not proof of a family connection. A name on a stone does not always mean that person is buried there. You can compare the proposed reading with the original photograph and see what remains uncertain.</p>
<p>Our field collection starts close to home, in Sperryville, Virginia. The aim is to help communities preserve and share the lives remembered in their cemeteries.</p>
<p><a href="{{ path('item_search') }}">Find a name or inscription →</a> · <a href="{{ path('about') }}">How MemorialAtlas works</a></p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
